{"type":"Film","id":"FR2023_198","slug":"fr2023-198-et-la-fete-continue","title":{"native":"Et la fête continue !","english":"And the Party Goes on"},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2023-11-15","year":2023},"filmType":"Fiction film","directors":[{"id":"Robert Guédiguian","slug":"robert-guediguian","name":"Robert Guédiguian","birthYear":1953,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]}],"genre":["Comedy","Drama"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://medias.unifrance.org/medias/209/33/270801/format_page/et-la-fete-continue.jpg","trailerUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZcbWl2uBLEw"},"synopsis":{"native":"Rosa est le cœur et l’âme de son quartier populaire du vieux Marseille. Elle partage son énergie débordante entre sa grande famille très unie, son travail d’infirmière et son engagement politique en faveur des plus modestes. Mais à l’approche de la retraite, ses illusions vacillent. Portée par la vitalité de ses proches et par sa rencontre avec Henri, elle va réaliser qu’il n’est jamais trop tard pour réaliser ses propres rêves, politiques et personnels.","english":"In the working-class district of old Marseilles, Rosa is the heart and soul of her community, a nurse and the matriarch of a large and close-knit family. But approaching retirement and surrounded by political inertia, she is feeling disillusioned. Until she meets Henri and realises it is never too late to fulfil her own political and personal dreams."},"production":[{"country":"France","share":"Majority coproducer"},{"country":"Italy","share":"Minority coproducer"}],"characters":[{"id":"FR2023_198_01","film":"FR2023_198","person":{"id":"Ariane Ascaride","slug":"ariane-ascaride","name":"Ariane Ascaride","birthYear":1954,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Female identifying","nationality":"France","awards":[]},"age":"3: Third Age (60-75)","gender":"Female identifying","sexuality":"Heterosexual","origin":"White Western European","class":"Middle class","profession":"Employed",